<title>JAPAN: Japan utility plans for new nuclear power reactors.</title>
<headline>Japan utility plans for new nuclear power reactors.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's power utilities are due to submit plans to a government advisory panel this fiscal year to build a combined five nuclear power reactors, the Ministry of International Trade and Industry said on Thursday.</p>
<p>A breakdown of the plans follows (in 10,000 kilowatts):</p>
<p>Operator			    capacity  start-up date</p>
<p>Tokyo Electric Power Co	  138	 March 2005</p>
<p>Tokyo Electric Power Co	  138	 March 2006</p>
<p>Chugoku Electric Power Co	137.3     March 2007</p>
<p>Chugoku Electric Power Co	137.3     2010 or after</p>
<p>Electric Power Development Co  138.3     October 2006</p>
<p>(All of the planned nuclear power reactors are boiling water reactors)</p>
</text>
